import Foundation

/// What the reader's own line tells of notices (#324), **as a real server sent it** — the Mastodon
/// 4.6.6 images `servers/compose.yml` pins, with its worker and its streaming service up
/// (`FEDIQO_SERVERS_WORKER=1 FEDIQO_SERVERS_STREAMING=1 make servers`) — asked on 2026-10-27 with
/// the seed's writer (`fediqo`), whose sign-in reads notices. The writer follows the second
/// person (`fediqo_other`) and not `fediqo_hidden`, and holds back private mentions from people it
/// does not follow (`for_private_mentions: filter`, the server's own default).
/// `MastodonNoticeLineSaysTests` asks the same again where those two are up.
///
/// ## What was asked, and what the server answered
///
/// | Asked | Mastodon 4.6.6 |
/// | ----- | -------------- |
/// | `GET /api/v1/streaming/user` by a sign-in holding `read:notifications` | 200: beside Home's events, `event: notification`, the notice whole as one line of JSON — the single read's shape (`id`, `type`, `created_at`, `group_key`, `account`, and `status` where it is about one) |
/// | the second person favours a post of the writer's, then boosts it | `notification` `favourite`, then `reblog` — each its own notice, with the `group_key` the gathered read would name it by (`favourite-<post>-<n>`), and the boost in Home as an `update` too |
/// | the second person names the writer | `notification` `mention`, `group_key` `ungrouped-<id>` |
/// | somebody the writer does not follow writes to the writer alone | **nothing on the line**: the server held it back (`notifications/requests` lists it), and the id it took (`141`) is skipped by the ids told |
/// | that person follows the writer | `notification` `follow`, no `status` |
/// | `GET /api/v1/streaming/user/notification` by a sign-in of `read:statuses` alone | 401 `{"error":"Access token does not have the required scopes"}` |
/// | `GET /api/v1/streaming/user` by the same | 200, and no `notification` ever (`MastodonLineCaptures`) |
enum MastodonNoticeLineCaptures {
    /// The writer's own line, the body verbatim from the first byte: the writer's post, a
    /// favourite, a boost of it (told as a notice and as a post in Home), a mention, a follow, and
    /// the post deleted. The private mention held back between them is not there.
    static let user = #"""
:)
